message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the article given under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "Supervisory gate control of the South Mirzachul main canal under supply shortage: code, data and results"
abstract: >-
  Code, input data, trained controllers and simulation results for the article
  "Neural supervisory gate control for sharing a supply shortage in a large
  irrigation main canal".
  The study tests whether a neural supervisory controller, trained by an evolution
  strategy on a one-dimensional Saint-Venant model of the 123.7-km South Mirzachul
  main canal (Uzbekistan), shares a supply shortage more equitably than a fixed rule
  and than a transparent rule optimized with the same algorithm and budget, using
  only the gates that the canal already has. It also tests the controllers under
  roughness uncertainty, measurement noise and equipment faults. The repository
  contains everything needed to rebuild Tables I–VI, Table B.1 (Supplementary Material) and Figs. 2–9 of the article.
  Code: MIT licence; data, results and figures: CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA.md).
